# SECURECODE v2.0

**Zero-Knowledge · End-to-End · Self-Destruct**

A secure anonymous messaging app. Write a message, get a one-time code. Share the code. Recipient redeems it — the message self-destructs.

---

## Features

- **Anonymous accounts** — random ID + 6-digit PIN, no email required
- **Persistent login** — server-side sessions survive browser restarts (30 days)
- **One-time codes** — `XXXX-XXXX` format, expire in 24h, destroyed on first read
- **Real backend** — Node.js + Express + SQLite (no external DB needed)
- **Code redemption without login** — recipients don't need an account
- **Mobile-first** — works great on phone browsers

---

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Tech |
|---|---|
| Backend | Node.js + Express |
| Database | SQLite via `better-sqlite3` |
| Sessions | `express-session` + `connect-sqlite3` |
| Auth | bcrypt PIN hashing |
| Frontend | Vanilla JS + SVG animations |

---

## Quick Start (Local)

```bash
# 1. Clone / download the repo
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/securecode.git
cd securecode

# 2. Install dependencies
npm install

# 3. Set up environment
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env — change SESSION_SECRET to something random

# 4. Run
npm start
# → http://localhost:3000
```

